# REQUIREMENTS.md — traceability matrix against the assignment brief

> Generated from `docs/REQUIREMENTS.md.tmpl`; every number resolves from `results/metrics.json` (which composes
> `results/parts/*.json`). One row per numbered requirement in sections 5-18 of the brief (every sub-bullet of
> 6.1, 14 and 15 included), plus the two section-2 behaviours the brief singles out. Written as a reviewer aid:
> the point is to confirm coverage in two minutes and to see where the evidence is thin.

**Status rule.** **MET** = the requirement is satisfied and an artifact in the *Evidenced* column shows it.
**PARTIAL** = addressed, but the measured evidence shows a shortfall, a stated target was missed, or the
mechanism's benefit is not demonstrated. **NOT DONE** = no artifact. No row is MET on an assertion; where the
evidence column would be empty the row would be NOT DONE (there are none). Documents: `T` =
`docs/TECHNICAL.md`, `R` = `docs/RESULTS.md`, `D` = `docs/DATA_CARD.md`. All data is synthetic; read the numbers as
properties of this simulator (`T` section 0).

## Scope: what the brief (section 4) says we did *not* have to build, and did not

| Out of scope in the brief | Built? | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| RAG, document retrieval | No | No retrieval-augmented component, vector store or document index; the runtime dependencies are numpy, pandas, pyarrow, scikit-learn, LightGBM, shap, scipy, rapidfuzz, h3, typer, pyyaml, matplotlib (`pyproject.toml`). The POI text embedding is a TF-IDF -> SVD feature block, not a retrieval index. |
| Chatbot, LLM-based travel assistant | No | No LLM or API client in `src/` or `pyproject.toml` (no API keys anywhere); explanations are deterministic templates with numeric fill-ins (`src/poi_rank/explain/templates.py`). |
| Complete itinerary generation, TSP/TSPTW, route optimization | No | The output is a ranked, weighted POI list with `planner_weight` for a downstream planner (`T` section 7); travel time appears only as a compatibility sub-score from haversine distance and an assumed mode speed, "not a routing engine" (`configs/scoring.yaml`). |
| Booking / payment | No | `booking` exists only as one of eight simulated *interaction types* in the synthetic log (`datagen/interactions.py`). |
| Frontend / UI | No | Terminal `make demo` and static files only. `docs/results.html` is a static, offline results explorer generated by `scripts/render_results_html.py` (no server, no product UI). |
| External service orchestration | No | CPU only, no network at run time (`README.md`). |

