## The three strongest and the three weakest results

**Strongest.**

1. **The ranker beats popularity and content cosine on unbiased labels.** NDCG@10 {{systems.lambdamart_ips.metrics.ndcg@10.mean|.4f}} against
   {{systems.popularity.metrics.ndcg@10.mean|.4f}} (popularity) and {{systems.content_cosine.metrics.ndcg@10.mean|.4f}} (cosine), paired Wilcoxon p={{wilcoxon.lambdamart_ips_vs_content_cosine.p_value|.2g}} against
   cosine, above cosine in {{~seed_vs_cosine}}. (The first tag had concluded the opposite; that conclusion was an artifact of a train/serve skew and is retracted in `T` section 5.1.)
2. **Hard constraints.** {{constraint_compatibility.n_hard_constraint_violations}} violations in {{constraint_compatibility.n_recommended}} recommended POIs against
   {{derived.dr1_hard_constraints.brief_additive_violations}} in {{derived.dr1_hard_constraints.n_trips}} trips with the brief's additive formula (DR1).
3. **Oracle-free retrieval that does not eliminate the long tail.** Candidate recall {{candidate_recall.overall.recall_mean|.3f}} overall /
   {{candidate_recall.long_tail.recall_mean|.3f}} long-tail against chance {{candidate_recall.by_stratum.overall.chance_recall|.3f}} / {{candidate_recall.by_stratum.long_tail.chance_recall|.3f}}; every selection was made on train-carved
   validation and the true-utility oracle only scored results.

**Weakest, each with the measurement behind the framing.**

1. **Long-tail precision {{longtail.precision|.3f}} against the 0.40 target** (share {{longtail.share|.3f}} against 0.25). The pool's own long-tail positive rate is
   {{derived.longtail_lift_over_base_rate.base_rate|.3f}}, so the served list is a {{derived.longtail_lift_over_base_rate.final_after_mmr|.2f}}x lift and the raw ranker a
   {{derived.longtail_lift_over_base_rate.raw_ranker|.2f}}x lift (raw precision {{longtail_stages.stages.1_raw_ranker_top10.long_tail_precision|.3f}}). Precision is lost mostly at the hard
   gate ({{longtail_stages.stages.2_after_hard_gate_raw_order.long_tail_precision|.3f}} after it), not in MMR (lambda {{longtail_stages.lambda_default}} was selected on validation; the sweep runs from
   {{derived.mmr_lift_lambda_0_5|.2f}}x at lambda 0.5 to {{derived.mmr_lift_lambda_1_0|.2f}}x at lambda 1). Experiment L raised it from {{l_holdout_report.shipped_config.longtail_precision|.3f}} but the 0.40 target, set a priori without
   reference to the base rate (`T` section 10.2), is not reached.
2. **Confidence values are barely informative about ranking quality.** Decile Spearman {{confidence_decile_validation.spearman_rho|.3f}} against at least 0.6 (it was
   {{confidence_diagnosis.post_fix.decile_spearman_recomputed|.3f}} before experiment L changed the served lists the confidence is averaged over); trip-level Spearman
   {{confidence_diagnosis.post_fix.trip_level_spearman_confidence_vs_ndcg|.3f}} before it. The earlier {{h_experiments.pre_fix_headline.confidence_decile_spearman|.3f}} came from leaked features; reweighting the confidence terms on
   holdout labels would be tuning on the holdout and was declined (`T` section 10.1).
3. **Archetype structure and the oracle ceiling.** Within/cross-archetype ratio {{personalization.archetype.within_cross_ratio|.2f}} against 2.0 (a perfect ranker gets
   {{scenario4_diagnosis.post_fix.holdout_personalization_reference.perfect_ranker_within_cross_ratio|.2f}}, so the target is unreachable by construction; the ranker recovers
   {{derived.within_cross_fraction_of_achievable|.0%}} of the achievable gap on the pre-L lists), and {{systems.lambdamart_ips.pct_of_ceiling_ndcg10|.1%}} of the candidate-level oracle ceiling against 70%: the taste estimator
   run over the TRUE semantic vectors reaches only {{representation.d9_within_trip.taste_estimator_alone.mean_within_trip_spearman|.3f}} within trip (`R` diagnoses).

Also MISSED and diagnosed in `R`: localness index Spearman {{localness_validation.spearman_rho|.3f}} against 0.6. Not missed but worth a reviewer's eye: the stated-preference factor overshoots
the outcome gradient (`T` section 3.1), and the selected MMR lambda turns the diversity re-rank off.
